{"skill":{"slug":"google-analytics-reporting","displayName":"Google Analytics"},"version":{"version":"1.0.5","createdAt":1780988951244,"changelog":"Add UTM attribution tags (utm_source=clawhub) to ClawLink branding links so visits from this skill page are tracked as a distinct traffic source.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":15655,"sha256":"445fd1d37a22ad9175848a502563cd1535d12cb025e56d4191f876da39806194","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2507,"sha256":"ef0789bb6b4df75530ccc63af5379fe22f5ed9160d17efb19a634e461aca5821","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789546202242,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8e796b07fa20980e226cc88736ae2dd4dec448c9fb78b297e399028650914b25","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8e796b07fa20980e226cc88736ae2dd4dec448c9fb78b297e399028650914b25","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780993010546},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":47,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789546202242},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Google Analytics skill is mostly coherent, but it enables a broad third-party ClawLink plugin with hosted OAuth credentials and write-capable analytics tools, so it needs careful review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Hosted ClawLink OAuth token custody and proxying are disclosed and purpose-aligned for GA4 integration, but they create a sensitive trust boundary for analytics data and account-management actions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation directs users to install the current clawhub:clawlink-plugin package, allowlist the whole plugin, and restart the OpenClaw gateway; the reviewed artifact does not include the plugin implementation or pin an immutable version.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill requires explicit confirmation and preview before writes, which is appropriate, but its invocation text is broad and key-event creation guidance is internally inconsistent with the later note that key events are read-only via API.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The tools.alsoAllow configuration and hosted OAuth connection persist beyond one chat, and the artifact does not document narrow tool-level allowlisting, token retention, or revocation controls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is GA4 reporting and inspection, which fits much of the tool reference, but the artifact also documents write-capable operations such as audience list creation, custom dimension/metric creation, property updates, and roll-up property creation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable trusting ClawLink with OAuth-backed access to the Google Analytics properties available to your Google account. Review the Google OAuth scopes and GA4 property permissions, avoid approving writes unless the preview exactly matches your intent, and know how to revoke the ClawLink Google connection if you stop using it.","findings":"[SDI-4] unexpected: The artifact does contain conflicting key-event guidance: early text discusses creating key events after confirmation, while the Notes section says key events require the Google Analytics UI. This appears to be a documentation/scope problem rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The write tools are disclosed in the tool reference and confirmation workflow, but they are broader than the top-level reporting-focused framing, so users may underestimate the management authority being enabled.\n[SQP-1] expected: The trigger language is broad but still centered on Google Analytics tasks; this was treated as over-invocation risk rather than hidden or unrelated behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: The gateway restart is part of setup and is disclosed immediately after the command block, but the impact would be clearer if stated before the commands.\n[T08] unexpected: Installing a plugin is expected for this skill, but the install command is not pinned to a reviewed immutable version, leaving the effective implementation dependent on the registry’s current package.\n[T05] unexpected: The artifact allowlists the whole ClawLink plugin while relying on hosted OAuth credentials and a live tool catalog, which is broader than a narrowly scoped GA4 reporting toolset.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789546202242}}}}}